  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Us Foods is the prime vendor shown on federal contract paperwork with $216M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Us Foods received 77 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.8M. Us Foods' obligations are down 15.3% year over year. Us Foods' work is concentrated in food-related NAICS. All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing accounts for $216M, Perishable Prepared Food Manufacturing accounts for $276K, and Food Service Contractors accounts for $10.9K. Us Foods sells primarily to the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $170M, followed by the Department of Defense at $32.8M and the Department of Agriculture at $7.5M. Us Foods' historical obligations rose from $143M in FY21 to $255M in FY25 before recording $216M in FY26 to date. Us Foods' FY2026 totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year totals.",
